  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 4,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.065,
            0.091,
            0.121,
            0.108
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Note"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.075,
            0.119,
            0.277,
            0.275
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Keep both the conical flasks on the digital weighing balance. It prevents the error caused by a small amount of solution that may remain stuck to the walls of the conical flask during transfer."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.076,
            0.276,
            0.259,
            0.355
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This reaction has been carried out in the open system, since no gas is formed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.108,
            0.492,
            0.297,
            0.511
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Pause and Ponder"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.075,
            0.525,
            0.285,
            0.665
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. A student burns 10 g of ethanol in an open beaker. After the reaction, no residue is left in the beaker. Does this mean the Law of Conservation of Mass is violated? Explain."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.075,
            0.667,
            0.285,
            0.777
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. When 20 g of hydrogen reacts completely with 160 g of oxygen, how much water is formed according to the Law of Conservation of Mass?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.315,
            0.087,
            0.89,
            0.14
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "When solutions of sodium sulfate and barium chloride are mixed, a white precipitate of barium sulfate is formed along with sodium chloride. It can be represented as —"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.315,
            0.145,
            0.885,
            0.163
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Sodium sulfate + Barium chloride Barium sulfate + Sodium chloride"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.314,
            0.165,
            0.889,
            0.216
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Based on the Activity 9.2, it was established that weight and hence, mass is conserved during a chemical change (chemical reaction)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.307,
            0.221,
            0.372,
            0.269
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.307,
                0.221,
                0.372,
                0.269
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_4_image_9.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.387,
            0.225,
            0.596,
            0.244
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think as a Scientist"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.36,
            0.249,
            0.876,
            0.302
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "You are given a chemical reaction in which zinc reacts with dilute hydrochloric acid to form zinc chloride and hydrogen gas. Zinc + Hydrochloric acid (dilute) Zinc chloride + Hydrogen"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.359,
            0.304,
            0.877,
            0.353
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Design and perform an experiment to test the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "hypothesis",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " that mass is conserved during the chemical reaction. You may use a set-up different from the one shown in Activity 9.2."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.315,
            0.373,
            0.89,
            0.46
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 9.1:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " In a group activity, students place 4.0 g of calcium carbonate with 2.92 g of hydrochloric acid in a closed container. After the reaction is over, they measured 1.76 g of carbon dioxide, 0.72 g of water, and 4.44 g of calcium chloride. Verify whether the Law of Conservation of Mass is obeyed or not."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.317,
            0.461,
            0.41,
            0.479
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solution:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.469,
            0.461,
            0.776,
            0.48
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Mass of calcium carbonate = 4.0 g"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.472,
            0.482,
            0.784,
            0.5
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Mass of hydrochloric acid = 2.92 g"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.316,
            0.501,
            0.533,
            0.519
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Total mass of reactants:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.588,
            0.501,
            0.783,
            0.52
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_4_equation_18.jpg",
          "content": "4.0\\;{\\rm g}+2.92\\;{\\rm g}=6.92\\;{\\rm g}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.495,
            0.521,
            0.783,
            0.539
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_4_equation_19.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm { M a s s ~ o f ~ c a r b o n ~ d i o x i d e } = 1 . 7 6 ~ \\mathrm { g }"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.575,
            0.54,
            0.783,
            0.558
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_4_equation_20.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm { { \\underline { { M a s s o f w a t e r } } } } = 0 . 7 2 \\; \\mathrm { { g } }"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.481,
            0.559,
            0.784,
            0.577
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_4_equation_21.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{M\\bar{a}s\\;of\\;clicium\\;clic/de}=4.44\\;\\mathrm{g}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.316,
            0.578,
            0.782,
            0.598
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Total mass of products: "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1.76 \\;  g  + 0.72 \\;  g  + 4.44 \\;  g  = 6.92 \\;  g"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 23,
          "bbox": [
            0.315,
            0.598,
            0.89,
            0.633
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Compare the total mass of reactants with the total mass of products."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 24,
          "bbox": [
            0.436,
            0.634,
            0.77,
            0.652
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Mass of reactants = Mass of products"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 25,
          "bbox": [
            0.315,
            0.654,
            0.769,
            0.672
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hence, the Law of Conservation of Mass is obeyed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 26,
          "bbox": [
            0.314,
            0.675,
            0.889,
            0.711
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 9.2:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " 12 g of carbon combines with 32 g of oxygen to form 44 g of carbon dioxide as per the given equation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 27,
          "bbox": [
            0.439,
            0.713,
            0.768,
            0.732
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_4_equation_27.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathtt { C a r b o n } + \\mathtt { O x y g e n } \\twoheadrightarrow \\mathtt { C a r b o n ~ d i o x i d e }"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 28,
          "bbox": [
            0.314,
            0.733,
            0.888,
            0.769
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If 2.4 g of carbon reacts completely with oxygen, how much carbon dioxide will be produced?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 29,
          "bbox": [
            0.315,
            0.771,
            0.888,
            0.806
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solution:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Given that 12 g of carbon reacts with 32 g of oxygen to give 44 g of carbon dioxide."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 30,
          "bbox": [
            0.316,
            0.806,
            0.813,
            0.84
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, 1 g of carbon will give "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "= \\frac { 4 4 } { 1 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " g of carbon dioxide"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 31,
          "bbox": [
            0.316,
            0.844,
            0.813,
            0.895
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, 2.4 g of carbon will give "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\begin{array} { r l } & { \\mathrm { ~ \\scriptsize ~ = ~ } \\frac { 4 4 } { 1 2 } \\times 2 . 4 \\mathrm { ~ g ~ } } \\\\ & { \\mathrm { ~ \\scriptsize ~ = ~ } 8 . 8 \\mathrm { ~ g ~ o f ~ c a r l } } \\end{array}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " bon dioxide"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 32,
          "bbox": [
            0.316,
            0.896,
            0.748,
            0.917
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hence, 8.8 g of carbon dioxide will be produced."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 33,
          "bbox": [
            0.075,
            0.942,
            0.115,
            0.96
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "166"
            }
          ]
        },
